IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-schedules`
IMPORT `voca-core`

-- Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2006 (NT) -- from the seat of THE PERSON ON WHOM THE LEVY IS IMPOSED (s 61): someone
-- found guilty of an offence in the Territory and not imprisoned for it, someone who pays an infringement notice (a
-- speeding fine, say), or someone against whom an enforcement order is made. "Must I pay the victims levy, and how much?
-- If I pay part of what I owe, what goes to the levy? Have I paid enough?" The levy funds the Victims Assistance Fund
-- that pays the awards in the victim's seat (voca-seat.l4). Every question is phrased as that person asks it, on facts
-- that person could state. The rules are in voca-core.l4; this module restates none, and every name here differs from
-- the other seats'.
--
-- The value of a revenue unit is not in the deposited texts: it is asked as a figure. The Fines and Penalties
-- (Recovery) Act 2001, which gives "infringement notice" and "enforcement order" their meanings, is not deposited
-- either: which of them happened is asked as a fact.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The victims levy -- the questions of a person found guilty of an offence, or paying an infringement notice`

§§ `s 61 and reg 26 -- the levy (asked only if I was found guilty of an offence, paid an infringement notice, or had an enforcement order made against me)`

@export Must I pay the levy for the Victims Assistance Fund, and how much (s 61(2), (3), (6), (9), (10); reg 26)?
GIVEN `how my offence was dealt with` IS A `How the offence was dealt with` @desc How the offence was dealt with: you were found guilty and not imprisoned for it (a fine or a bond, say); found guilty and imprisoned for it; you paid the amount in an infringement notice (an on-the-spot fine); or an enforcement order was made against you for an unpaid fine
      `the law my offence was against` IS A `Law of the offence` @desc The law the offence was against: the Return to Work Act 1986; the Public Sector Employment and Management Act 1993; the Public and Environmental Health Act 2011; the Litter Act 1972; Part 12 of the Australian Road Rules (the stopping and parking rules); a local council by-law; the Territory Parks and Wildlife Conservation By-Laws 1984; a Charles Darwin University by-law or rule; another law in force in the Northern Territory (a speeding offence, say); or a law not in force in the Territory
      `a local council prosecuted me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you were found guilty: whether the prosecution was brought by a local government council; otherwise no
      `what I am` IS A `Kind of person levied` @desc Whether you are an adult (18 or more), a child, or a body corporate such as a company
      `I was prosecuted on indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you were found guilty: whether the offence was prosecuted on indictment (tried as an indictable offence); otherwise no
      `the value of one revenue unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of one revenue unit, in Australian dollars, for the financial year the levy is imposed in (it is fixed outside the deposited texts: give the figure)
GIVETH A `Levy answer`
DECIDE `Must I pay the victims levy` IS
    `the s 61 answer for` `how my offence was dealt with` `the law my offence was against` `a local council prosecuted me` `what I am` `I was prosecuted on indictment` `the value of one revenue unit`

@export If I pay part of what I owe on my infringement notice, how much of my payment goes to the levy first (s 61(8))?
GIVEN `the amount I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you pay towards the infringement notice, in Australian dollars
      `the levy I still owe` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy you still owe for the notice, in Australian dollars (see the levy question; 0 if none or already paid)
GIVETH AN `Appropriation answer`
DECIDE `How much of my payment goes to the levy` IS
    `the s 61(8) answer for` `the amount I pay` `the levy I still owe`

@export Have I paid enough for the levy not to stand in the way of my immunity from prosecution for the offence (s 61(7))?
GIVEN `the amount in my infringement notice or enforcement order` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the infringement notice or enforcement order requires you to pay, not counting the levy, in Australian dollars
      `the levy on me in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc The levy imposed on you, in Australian dollars (see the levy question; 0 if none)
      `what I have paid so far` IS A NUMBER @desc The total you have paid so far on the notice or order, levy included, in Australian dollars
GIVETH AN `Immunity answer`
DECIDE `Have I paid enough for immunity from prosecution` IS
    `the s 61(7) answer for` `the amount in my infringement notice or enforcement order` `the levy on me in dollars` `what I have paid so far`
